{
  "note": "Viewer-to-host signaling messages that open and confirm a WSS media session. Each message is the exact JSON object a viewer sends; builtBy lists the viewers whose builder is checked against it. A viewer builds the message with the fixture's own values, so the test fails when a field, a value or the key set drifts.",
  "unpinned": {
    "browser": "worker/public/receiver.js builds first-frame, keyframe, monitor and follow messages inline in sendControl calls; its start message is assembled in the codec session. Naming these literals in a test needs a source slice or a refactor of a file owned by the viewer lane.",
    "kotlin": "android Session.kt builds the same messages inline; no builder function to call from a test."
  },
